1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,520
If you shattered your wrist,

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,680
imagine gluing the bones back together.

3
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:05,420
Researchers actually did it.

4
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:07,095
They developed an experimental glue

5
00:00:07,135 --> 00:00:09,530
inspired by oysters sticking to rocks.

6
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:11,005
It grips bone even inside

7
00:00:11,045 --> 00:00:12,550
a wet, bloody wound.

8
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:14,090
In one reported wrist case,

9
00:00:14,130 --> 00:00:15,805
surgeons secured the broken pieces

10
00:00:15,845 --> 00:00:17,370
in just three minutes.

11
00:00:17,410 --> 00:00:19,400
The fracture still needed months to heal.

12
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:20,820
But as new bone grows,

13
00:00:20,860 --> 00:00:22,750
the glue gradually disappears.

14
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:23,830
Your body replaces

15
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:25,570
the stuff holding you together.

